        "description": "The proposed projects do not stem from a mere formal intuition, but rather from a careful analysis of the village's needs and urban voids. Acknowledging the spatial fragmentation of the settlement, the chosen approach goes beyond simple restoration, aiming instead for a true adaptive reuse and functional conversion of the existing structures.<br><br>The goal is to trigger a chain reaction for the regeneration of the entire village through \"urban acupuncture\" interventions. Avoiding a massive, monolithic approach, the strategy is divided into four intervention lots, differing in typology and function, yet synergistically connected.<br><br>This subdivision also ensures the economic sustainability of the overall process, allowing for a phased development that can easily adapt to the client's actual financial resources.<br>"
      }
    }
  ],
